# Arduino DC Motor Control Project

## Project Description
This project demonstrates how to control four DC motors using an Arduino Uno and an L293D motor driver. The motors perform a sequence of movements automatically. The system is designed to simulate the movement of a simple robotic vehicle.

## Components
- Arduino Uno
- L293D Motor Driver
- 4 DC Motors
- Breadboard
- 9V Battery
- Jumper Wires

## Features
- Move forward for 30 seconds.
- Turn for 60 seconds.
- Stop for 60 seconds.
- Repeat the sequence continuously.

## Circuit
The Arduino sends control signals to the L293D motor driver, which powers and controls the four DC motors. The breadboard is used to distribute power and simplify the wiring.

## Software
- Arduino IDE
- Tinkercad Circuits

## How to Run
1. Connect all components according to the circuit diagram.
2. Upload the Arduino code.
3. Power the circuit.
4. The motors will move forward, turn, stop, and repeat the cycle automatically.

